# Swipe design loop

If `design/handoff/<task-id>/TASK.md` exists for this run, read it before editing. It is the assignment.

## Ownership
- Pixel: `design/visual/**`, `design/handoff/**/TASK.md`, spec-named `assets/**`.
- Agent: `scripts/**`, `scenes/**`, `.import`, `REPORT.md`.
- Do not overwrite PNG bytes. Stay inside the TASK.md "Files you may touch" list.

## Spec
- Numbers live in `design/visual/layouts/<id>.layout.json`. JSON wins over the screen markdown; flag the disagreement in REPORT.md.
- Palette, type roles, outline widths, and nine-slices belong in `design/visual/`. A layout may name a role. Do not invent a hex or a size.
- Set each built node's `name` to its JSON `id`.
- Two readings that would change a rect, number, state, target, or owned file: write questions in `REPORT.md` (tag [Pixel]/[Jam]/[Nathan]), status `BLOCKED`, and stop.

## Do not
- No new font files and no generated bitmap fonts. Use `ThemeDB.fallback_font` only (until a tokens file under `design/visual/` names a font).
- No player-facing copy edits. Jam owns `data/player-copy.json`. No "Tier" or "owner" in UI text.
- No stretching, hiding, or recoloring art to fake a missing asset. Ask in REPORT.md with path, native size, 4Ã— nearest, pivot, loop, palette.
- No new dependencies, no paid or non-CC0 assets, no save-format changes, no merges, no pushes.
- Never commit to `cabin-overhaul-1` directly. Where to build and how Nathan playtests: see `.cursor/rules/playtest-approve.mdc`.

## New card art
- A catalog entry that needs new art (`flags.art` false, or notes say it needs unique art): after saving the catalog, run `tools\request_art.cmd <id> [<id> ...]` once per batch. `art ping not configured` is fine; carry on.
- Keep the placeholder. Do not draw PNGs. Do not add those ids to `ITEM_PNG` / `MONSTER_PNG` in `scripts/dungeon_art.gd`. Pixel draws and wires them.
- When the batch is done, commit it (data, scripts, docs) so Pixel can wire art without clashing.

